<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mughith al-Din Tughrilshah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1225</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Tughrilshah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mughith al-Din Tughrilshah was a prince of the Seljuk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> and a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kilij-arslan-ii">Kilij Arslan II</a>. In 1202 his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleymanshah-ii">Süleymanshah II</a> gave him <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erzurum">Erzurum</a>, taken from the Saltukids, and he ruled it as a largely independent principality until his death. His son Jahanshah succeeded him but lost Erzurum to the Rum Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kayqubad-i">Kayqubad I</a> around 1230.</p></div>
